          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %em étale homotopy
            can be understood as a vast generalization of the following classical fact.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve+theorem"} nerve theorem
            says that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+topological+space"} paracompact topological space
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/good+cover"} good cover
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            by open subsets, then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            obtained from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+nerve"} Cech nerve
            of the covering by degreewise contracting all connected components to a point, presents the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            here is more generally a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+contractible+space"} locally contractible space
            there is in general no notion of “good” enough open cover anymore. Instead, one can consider the above kind of construction for
            %em all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercovers"} hypercovers
            and take the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
            over the resulting simplicial sets. The classical theorem by
            %a{:href => "#ArtinMazur"} Artin-Mazur
            states that this still gives the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            The construction itself, however, makes sense for arbitrary topological spaces and in fact for arbitrary
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sites"} sites
          %p
            In the literature, particularly the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+site"} étale site
            is often considered and “étale homotopy” is often implicitly understood to take place over this site.
          %p
            But the concept is much more general. In particular, one can understand the construction of the limit over contractions of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercovers"} hypercovers
            as a presentation of naturally defined
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functors"} (∞,1)-functors
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos+theory"} (∞,1)-topos theory
          %p
            Notably, if the given site is a a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+%E2%88%9E-connected+site"} locally ∞-connected site
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
            that presents the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+%E2%88%9E-groupoid+in+a+locally+%E2%88%9E-connected+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} fundamental ∞-groupoid in a locally ∞-connected (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+homotopy+groups+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} geometric homotopy groups in an (∞,1)-topos
          %p
            Even more generally, étale homotopy give the notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} shape of an (∞,1)-topos
          %h2#Examples Examples
          %h3#chevalley_groups_and_galois_groups Chevalley groups and Galois groups
          %p
            For the special case of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groups"} fundamental groups
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley+fundamental+groups"} Chevalley fundamental groups
          %p
            The étale fundamental group of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            is its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolute+Galois+group"} absolute Galois group
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "Galois+theory#StatementOfMainTheorem"} Galois theory – Statement of the main result
          %h3#tale_contractibility Étale contractibility
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
              0, then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+line"} affine line
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi k
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}^1_k
              is étale
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+homotopy+type"} contractible
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+number"} positive
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#HSS13"}> HSS 13, section 1
            )
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraically+closed+field"} algebraically closed field
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+number"} positive
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+variety"} smooth variety
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              which is étale
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+homotopy+type"} contractible
              is the point
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spec
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(k)
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-connected+object+of+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} 2-connected
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#HSS13"}> HSS 13, theorem 1
            )
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+homology"} Čech homology
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+fundamental+group"} algebraic fundamental group
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anabelian+geometry"} anabelian geometry
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+topos"}> étale topos
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pro-%C3%A9tale+topos"} pro-étale topos
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+cohomology"} étale cohomology
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p Original articles include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Artin"}> Michael Artin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barry+Mazur"} Barry Mazur
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homotopy of varieties in the etale topology
            %li
              %p#ArtinMazur
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Artin"}> Michael Artin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barry+Mazur"} Barry Mazur
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Étale Homotopy
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Friedlander"}> Eric Friedlander
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Fibrations in étale homotopy theory
                    %a{:href => "http://archive.numdam.org/ARCHIVE/PMIHES/PMIHES_1973__42_/PMIHES_1973__42__5_0/PMIHES_1973__42__5_0.pdf"} (numdam)
              %p Inst. des Haut. Études Scient., 42, (1973), 5 – 46.
          %p
            The modern perspective from the point of view of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structures on simplicial presheaves
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Isaksen01
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Isaksen"}> Daniel Isaksen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Étale realization of the
                    = succeed "-homotopy" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi 𝔸
                              %mn 1
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}^1
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/K-theory/0495/"} K-theory archive
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G.+Quick"}> G. Quick
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Stable étale realization and étale cobordism
              %p 214 (2007), 730–760.
          %p
            and fully abstractly from the point of view of
            = succeed "-theory" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} shape of an (∞,1)-topos
          %ul
            %li#Hoyois13a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marc+Hoyois"}> Marc Hoyois
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Higher Galois theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://math.mit.edu/~hoyois/papers/highergalois.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            and (
            %a{:href => "#Hoyois13b"}> Hoyois 13b, section 1
            ).
          %p and in, where a comparison theorem over the complex numbers is also proven:
          %ul
            %li#Carchedi15
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dave+Carchedi"}> Dave Carchedi
              ,
              %em On the étale homotopy type of higher stacks
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1511.07830"}> arXiv:1511.07830
              )
          %p An introduction is in
          %ul
            %li
              Tomer Schlank, Alexei Skorobogatov,
              = succeed "." do
                %em A very brief introduction to étale homotopy
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.ma.imperial.ac.uk/~anskor/SCHLANK-SKOROBOGATOV.pdf"} pdf
          %p Lecture notes on the étale fundamental group are in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Milne"}> James Milne
                , section 4 of
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lectures+on+%C3%89tale+Cohomology"} Lectures on Étale Cohomology
              %p
                Generalization to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+schemes"} simplicial schemes
                is discussed in
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Friedlander"}> Eric Friedlander
                , 1982,
                %em Étale homotopy of simplicial schemes
                , volume 104 of Annals of Mathematics Studies , Princeton University Press, Princeton, N.J.
          %p More on this is in
          %ul
            %li
              Michael Misamore,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Étale homotopy types and bisimplicial hypercovers
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.intlpress.com/HHA/v15/n1/a2/"} web
          %h3#examples_and_applications Examples and applications
          %ul
            %li#Hoyois13b
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marc+Hoyois"}> Marc Hoyois
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The étale-symmetric Künneth theorem
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://math.mit.edu/~hoyois/papers/etalekunneth.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+characteristic"} positive characteristic
            is in
          %ul
            %li#HSS13
              Armin Holschbach, Johannes Schmidt,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jakob+Stix"} Jakob Stix
              %em Étale contractible varieties in positive characteristic
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1310.2784"}> arXiv:1310.2784
              )
          %p
            Étale homotopy type of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stacks+of+curves"} moduli stacks of curves
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              Paola Frediani, Frank Neumann,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Étale homotopy types of moduli stacks of algebraic curves with symmetries
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0404387"} arXiv:math/0404387
